# Red Ward's "This effect doesn't remove this Aura" spares it from its own protection only: another instance of
# protection from red still removes it once it is red (CR 702.16n, 704.5m). Red Ward enchants a creature, any
# player's (CR 303.4a): Bot1 cannot cast it on its Mox Jet (the refusal) but enchants Bot2's Sea Sprite, which has
# protection from red of its own. While the Ward is white it stays; Painter's Servant naming red makes it red
# (CR 105.3), and the Sprite's protection puts it into Bot1's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Red Ward
Painter's Servant
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Sea Sprite
Island x12

